  "assumptions": [
    "Maturity is prototype, so the stack follows the simplest viable architecture: an application calling a model API, plus the requested monitoring component.",
    "The model may be a third-party API or a self-hosted model; both are treated as a single external model endpoint at this stage.",
    "Monitoring tracks latency (time to first token, per-token time, total latency), token volumes, and request rates per source guidance, but no automated retraining or release loop exists yet.",
    "No guardrails, routers, caching, or write actions are included; those are later additions and out of scope for a prototype."
  ],
